<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Grand Duchy of Baden</h1><p class="st-meta">1806 CE – 1918 CE · capital Karlsruhe</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">South-western German grand duchy known for its liberal constitution, its revolutionaries of 1848-49 and its role as a model constitutional state.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-frederick-grand-duke-of-baden">Charles Frederick</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> in 1806 and became grand duke, gaining Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breisgau">Breisgau</a>, mediatised lands and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a> region. His long, narrow state stretched from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstanz">Constance</a> along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The constitution of 1818 created one of the most liberal parliaments in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> revolutionaries of 1848, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-hecker">Friedrich Hecker</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-struve">Gustav Struve</a>, were defeated, and in 1849 the army mutinied and the grand duke fled until Prussian troops restored him. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-grand-duke-of-baden">Frederick I</a>, from 1856, Baden became a liberal model state. Universities at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freiburg-im-breisgau">Freiburg</a> and industry at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karlsruhe">Karlsruhe</a> flourished.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1866 but joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a> in 1871. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-grand-duke-of-baden">Grand Duke Frederick II</a> abdicated in November 1918, and the state became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-baden">Republic of Baden</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/grand-duchy-of-baden.jpg" alt="Grand Duchy of Baden" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Gro%C3%9Fherzogtum_Baden_(1891%E2%80%931918).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1806 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Karlsruhe</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles Frederick, Leopold, Frederick I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Alemannic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Großherzogtum Baden</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1862&amp;focus=grand-duchy-of-baden" aria-label="Grand Duchy of Baden on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4874 467 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Grand Duchy of Baden lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5194 723L5208 771M5194 723L5200 712M5194 723L5212 705M5194 723L5194 723M5194 723L5199 691M5194 723L5199 691M5194 723L5300 622M5194 723L5194 723M5194 723L5199 757M5194 723L5219 702M5194 723L5197 764M5194 723L5184 744M5194 723L5178 757"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5208 771h0M5200 712h0M5212 705h0M5194 723h0M5199 691h0M5199 691h0M5300 622h0M5194 723h0M5199 757h0M5219 702h0M5197 764h0M5184 744h0M5178 757h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d